    "content": "---\r\nname: ai-champion-onboarding-kit\r\ndisplayName: AI Champion Onboarding Kit\r\ntagline: Generate an onboarding kit for department AI champions with training materials and rollout playbook.\r\ndescription: |\r\n  Creates a complete onboarding package for department-level AI champions who will\r\n  drive adoption within their teams. Includes a modular training curriculum (AI\r\n  fundamentals, tool-specific training, change management, security), a week-by-week\r\n  rollout playbook, success metrics with targets, and ready-to-use templates for\r\n  workshops, surveys, and team communications.\r\ndepartment:\r\n  - AI Enablement Leaders\r\n  - Engineering\r\nuse_cases:\r\n  - Onboarding\r\n  - Documentation\r\n  - Workflow Automation\r\ntools_required:\r\n  - Google Drive MCP\r\n  - Notion MCP\r\nagents_compatible:\r\n  - Claude / Claude Code\r\n  - Cursor\r\n  - Windsurf\r\n  - ChatGPT\r\n  - GitHub Copilot\r\n  - Any MCP-compatible agent\r\nauthor: Webrix\r\nverified: true\r\nupdatedAt: 2026-02-24\r\nversion: 1.0.0\r\nexampleInput: |\r\n  Organization: E-commerce company, 200 engineers across 10 teams\r\n  AI tools approved: GitHub Copilot, Claude Team, Cursor\r\n  Champions to onboard: 10 (one per team)\r\n  Timeline: Q2 2026 rollout\r\nexampleOutput: |\r\n  AI Champion Onboarding Kit — Q2 2026\r\n\r\n  WELCOME PACKET\r\n  Role: Department AI Champion\r\n  Time commitment: 3-4 hours/week (first month), 1-2 hours/week (ongoing)\r\n  Reports to: AI Program Lead (Sarah Chen)\r\n\r\n  TRAINING CURRICULUM\r\n  ✅ Module 1: AI Fundamentals (30 min) — Complete by Week 1\r\n  ✅ Module 2: Tool Training (3 sessions × 60 min) — Copilot, Claude, Cursor\r\n  ✅ Module 3: Leading AI Adoption (45 min) — Change management\r\n  ✅ Module 4: Security & Compliance (30 min) — Data classification\r\n\r\n  ROLLOUT TIMELINE\r\n  Week 1:  Champion completes training, gets certified\r\n  Week 2:  Team baseline survey (current AI usage + interest)\r\n  Week 3:  Kickoff workshop — live demo + hands-on exercises\r\n  Week 4:  1:1 pair programming sessions with interested members\r\n  Week 5-6: Weekly office hours (drop-in Q&A)\r\n  Week 7-8: First metrics report + share team wins\r\n\r\n  SUCCESS TARGETS (90 days)\r\n  Adoption: 70% | Training: 100% | Satisfaction: 4+/5 | Time saved: 5 hrs/week\r\n\r\n  Generated: Google Drive folder with 6 documents (slides, templates, surveys)\r\n  Generated: Notion workspace with rollout tracker and knowledge base\r\n---\r\n\r\n# AI Champion Onboarding Kit\r\n\r\nGenerate an onboarding kit for department AI champions including training materials, success metrics, and rollout playbook.\r\n\r\n**Integrations:** Google Drive, Notion\r\n\r\n## When to Use\r\n\r\n- The user is setting up an AI champions program\r\n- A team needs to identify and onboard AI advocates within departments\r\n- The user mentions \"AI champion\", \"AI advocate\", \"train the trainer\", or \"AI rollout\"\r\n- Organizations want a grassroots approach to AI adoption\r\n\r\n## Steps\r\n\r\n### Step 1: Define the Champion Role\r\n\r\nHelp the user define the AI Champion responsibilities:\r\n\r\n| Responsibility | Description |\r\n|---------------|-------------|\r\n| **Advocate** | Promote AI tool usage and share success stories within their team |\r\n| **Trainer** | Run hands-on workshops and pair-programming sessions with AI tools |\r\n| **Support** | Be the first point of contact for AI tool questions in their department |\r\n| **Feedback** | Collect feedback from their team and relay to the central AI team |\r\n| **Compliance** | Ensure their team follows the AI usage policy |\r\n| **Metrics** | Track and report adoption metrics for their department |\r\n\r\n### Step 2: Create Training Materials\r\n\r\nGenerate a training curriculum:\r\n\r\n**Module 1: AI Fundamentals (30 min)**\r\n- How LLMs work (high-level, non-technical)\r\n- Prompt engineering basics\r\n- Understanding AI limitations and hallucinations\r\n- Data privacy considerations\r\n\r\n**Module 2: Tool-Specific Training (60 min per tool)**\r\n- Setup and configuration walkthrough\r\n- Top 10 workflows for each approved tool\r\n- Tips and tricks from power users\r\n- Common pitfalls to avoid\r\n\r\n**Module 3: Leading AI Adoption (45 min)**\r\n- Change management principles\r\n- Handling resistance and skepticism\r\n- Measuring and communicating success\r\n- Escalation paths for issues\r\n\r\n**Module 4: Security & Compliance (30 min)**\r\n- AI usage policy overview\r\n- Data classification quick reference\r\n- What to do when things go wrong\r\n- Audit and reporting responsibilities\r\n\r\n### Step 3: Build the Rollout Playbook\r\n\r\nCreate a week-by-week rollout plan:\r\n\r\n| Week | Activity | Champion Action |\r\n|------|----------|----------------|\r\n| 1 | Champion Training | Complete all training modules, get certified |\r\n| 2 | Team Assessment | Survey team on current AI usage and interest |\r\n| 3 | Kickoff Workshop | Run first team workshop on primary AI tool |\r\n| 4 | Pair Programming | Schedule 1:1 sessions with interested team members |\r\n| 5-6 | Open Office Hours | Weekly drop-in sessions for questions |\r\n| 7-8 | Measure & Report | Collect first metrics, share wins |\r\n| 9-12 | Sustain & Scale | Monthly workshops, advanced topics, peer sharing |\r\n\r\n### Step 4: Define Success Metrics\r\n\r\n| Metric | Target (by 90 days) | How to Measure |\r\n|--------|---------------------|----------------|\r\n| Adoption Rate | 70% of team actively using AI tools | Tool login data / SSO |\r\n| Training Completion | 100% of team completes Module 1 | LMS or sign-off sheet |\r\n| Satisfaction Score | 4+ out of 5 | Monthly pulse survey |\r\n| Time Saved | 5+ hours/week per developer | Self-reported survey |\r\n| Support Tickets | <3 escalations per month | Jira/Slack tracking |\r\n\r\n### Step 5: Generate Deliverables\r\n\r\nCreate in Google Drive or Notion:\r\n\r\n1. **Champion Welcome Packet** — Role description, expectations, time commitment, support resources\r\n2. **Training Slide Decks** — One per module, ready to present\r\n3. **Workshop Templates** — Hands-on exercises for team workshops\r\n4. **Survey Templates** — Pre-adoption baseline and monthly pulse surveys\r\n5. **Metrics Dashboard Template** — Spreadsheet for tracking department-level metrics\r\n6. **Communication Templates** — Email templates for team announcements, success stories, tips of the week\r\n\r\n## Output\r\n\r\nDeliver:\r\n- Complete onboarding packet (Google Drive folder or Notion workspace)\r\n- Training curriculum with slide templates\r\n- Rollout playbook with timeline\r\n- Metrics tracking spreadsheet\r\n- Communication templates\r\n",
